Z||000000||btoth||12-03-2001||06:37 PM||||I was in Border's Book Store yesterday and saw on the discount book table the "American Car Encyclopedia".  (Or something like that.)  Anyway, they had pictures of each model and a pretty lengthy write-up (and a positive one too!).  I don't remember most of it (I didn't buy it), but they did say something about them being collected and "mini muscle cars" (in referance to the V6).  Maybe the library has it...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||NOCONES||12-04-2001||12:39 AM||||Cool find, i think i've seen that one.. but i also saw one that was a lemon book.. and it had a write up on the fiero.. but don't worry.. i assume it only ment the 4-cyl <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by btoth:<BR><B> but they did say something about them being collected and "mini muscle cars" (in referance to the V6).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Why do people do that.. all us simply 4-cyl owners know that our cars or slow, so stop making reference to it.  I mean i don't think my car is a muscle car<BR>j/k<P>but still.. people do do stuff like  that alot, and it discourages me as a 4-cyl owner from feeling involved in the Group as a fellow enthusiast<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||LoW_KeY||12-04-2001||11:40 AM||||heck thats why you gotta buy more fieros.. throw a few 6's and 4's in there maybe even a V8   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I had a 4 and loved the car I didn't care what anyone thought.<P>I know Joe on this board has a 87 4cylinder 5spd that thing is rather snappy, great looking car too! I must say gadgets galore on that guys car.<P>On a serious note dont be discouraged, I think the 6 didn't bring me as much fun as my 4, I think the 4 cylinder put the smack down on a lot of people in my city and made them realize whoa.. heck if I found an Indy for the right price I'd buy it, to bad they didn't keep the actual 4 they had in it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I mean they did that turbo 89? T/A and left it as it was, but hey 4 cylinders are good in my book.<P>-KC<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FierFormula88   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kcbanner.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by LoW_KeY (edited 12-04-2001).]||||reg||1
